ly closed paper seed packets; one small open packet shows a few dry wheat and barley grains, making the actual seed backup visible. Only supporting detail is a receding shelf of identical unmarked archive cartons and a heavy insulated doorway. This depicts careful withdrawal of a depositor's own partial backup, not an apocalypse or destruction of the collection. No sprouting plants inside the frozen storage, no floodwater reaching the seeds, no broken vault, no giant ice crystals, no written labels or temperatures anywhere. One coherent cool storage interior expressed through warm ivory paper, subdued sage shadows and quiet watercolor, not a photo of a specific dated retrieval.",
